710
00:31:20,470 --> 00:31:24,330
So you see that yellow block
now submits the solution

711
00:31:24,330 --> 00:31:27,050
to the private set of tests.

712
00:31:27,050 --> 00:31:30,650
And based on that, it will go
and try to improve the model now

713
00:31:30,650 --> 00:31:33,890
that the solution
is looking better.

714
00:31:33,890 --> 00:31:36,730
One of the key aspects
of their approach

715
00:31:36,730 --> 00:31:38,930
was that, during
iteration, the public test

716
00:31:38,930 --> 00:31:41,810
will provide immediate
feedback and will help it

717
00:31:41,810 --> 00:31:43,870
do better solution development.

718
00:31:43,870 --> 00:31:47,310
But this is a small subset
for faster iteration,

719
00:31:47,310 --> 00:31:51,290
and this is basically allowing
the model to guide and get

720
00:31:51,290 --> 00:31:53,970
better solution, while the
private tests are completely

721
00:31:53,970 --> 00:31:55,630
hidden during the
generation process.

722
00:31:55,630 --> 00:31:58,090
So basically, this
separation allows

723
00:31:58,090 --> 00:32:02,190
it to not go train
on the public test,

724
00:32:02,190 --> 00:32:05,230
but only use the private test
as the way to get signal.

725
00:32:05,230 --> 00:32:08,810
And this is one way in which
the model cannot simply memorize

726
00:32:08,810 --> 00:32:12,790
the test outputs, because it's
getting the execution feedback.

727
00:32:12,790 --> 00:32:15,710
So this, they found, is
a very useful innovation

728
00:32:15,710 --> 00:32:17,710
in the self-improvement loop.

729
00:32:17,710 --> 00:32:20,870
A second innovation-- so I
will actually not make you

730
00:32:20,870 --> 00:32:23,250
go through the details
of this RL algorithm.

731
00:32:23,250 --> 00:32:24,733
This is basically PPO.

732
00:32:24,733 --> 00:32:26,150
But the one thing
I want to stress

733
00:32:26,150 --> 00:32:28,210
is that when you're in
