1242
00:55:46,220 --> 00:55:48,200
But overall, you have to
find the right balance

1243
00:55:48,200 --> 00:55:50,480
between these two.

1244
00:55:50,480 --> 00:55:51,840
Thank you.

1245
00:55:51,840 --> 00:55:52,760
Yes.

1246
00:55:52,760 --> 00:55:55,840
Let me go back to step
1 of the Constitution AI

1247
00:55:55,840 --> 00:55:57,500
to the supervised learning part.

1248
00:55:57,500 --> 00:56:00,080
So it said in the
slides that we want

1249
00:56:00,080 --> 00:56:01,920
to fine-tune on
the data generated

1250
00:56:01,920 --> 00:56:03,840
by self-critiquing relations.

1251
00:56:03,840 --> 00:56:06,960
So I want to understand
whether this just simply means

1252
00:56:06,960 --> 00:56:08,600
that we want to just
reinforce the log

1253
00:56:08,600 --> 00:56:13,000
likelihoods over literally
the generations, the rollouts

1254
00:56:13,000 --> 00:56:17,280
of the L, of the
original policy of L.

1255
00:56:17,280 --> 00:56:19,520
So basically, we just ask
it to critique itself,

1256
00:56:19,520 --> 00:56:24,340
and then we just fine-tune this
sampled rollouts so that they're

1257
00:56:24,340 --> 00:56:24,840
more likely.

1258
00:56:24,840 --> 00:56:29,200
That's what this stage
is basically [INAUDIBLE]?

1259
00:56:29,200 --> 00:56:34,660
It's a stage that's used
in a lot of other things

1260
00:56:34,660 --> 00:56:35,520
that you will see.

1261
00:56:35,520 --> 00:56:38,700
But what this is basically
is doing a set of--

1262
00:56:38,700 --> 00:56:40,980
these are traces
that it's generated.

1263
00:56:40,980 --> 00:56:42,040
It's based on reasoning.

1264
00:56:42,040 --> 00:56:44,320
You want it to follow a
certain set of principles,

1265
00:56:44,320 --> 00:56:46,000
and then it critiqued itself.

1266
00:56:46,000 --> 00:56:47,860
It revised itself,
and it got fine-tuned

1267
00:56:47,860 --> 00:56:49,160
on this set of traces.

1268
00:56:49,160 --> 00:56:53,360
I mean, if you were training
it for thinking, for example,

1269
00:56:53,360 --> 00:56:56,100
these would be the
reasoning traces.

1270
00:56:56,100 --> 00:56:58,860
So I think being trained
on-- it's being fine-tuned

1271
00:56:58,860 --> 00:57:01,060
on those reasoning traces,

1272
00:57:01,060 --> 00:57:03,700
But I guess it's interesting
that there's not really

1273
00:57:03,700 --> 00:57:05,660
an explicit feedback--

1274
00:57:05,660 --> 00:57:06,700
There is no feedback.

1275
00:57:06,700 --> 00:57:08,700
--because it's just
asked to do this thing,

1276
00:57:08,700 --> 00:57:12,380
and then we just fine-tune it
over what it has tried to do.

1277
00:57:12,380 --> 00:57:14,380
But as long as the
fine-tuning is not very large

1278
00:57:14,380 --> 00:57:17,500
scale-- it's much smaller
than what the base model was

1279
00:57:17,500 --> 00:57:19,100
initially trained
on-- it will not

1280
00:57:19,100 --> 00:57:21,820
lose its initial capabilities,
but the distribution of what

1281
00:57:21,820 --> 00:57:24,180
it will output, will
start to get biased

1282
00:57:24,180 --> 00:57:28,420
towards this set of responses.

1283
00:57:28,420 --> 00:57:31,540
So I'm pretty sure the
foundation [INAUDIBLE].

1284
00:57:34,920 --> 00:57:36,080
The AI feedback stuff?

1285
00:57:36,080 --> 00:57:36,580
Yes.

1286
00:57:36,580 --> 00:57:38,320
How do we evaluate
