1292
00:57:48,760 --> 00:57:52,040
to make sure that the preference
model will do a great job.

1293
00:57:52,040 --> 00:57:54,080
So you do want to
have some human.

1294
00:57:54,080 --> 00:57:55,680
But typically, what
you'll do is you

1295
00:57:55,680 --> 00:57:57,460
will do a lot of AI feedback.

1296
00:57:57,460 --> 00:57:58,960
But for the preference
model, you'll

1297
00:57:58,960 --> 00:58:02,080
also get it to give some
scores on set of things

1298
00:58:02,080 --> 00:58:03,900
and then match it with humans.

1299
00:58:03,900 --> 00:58:06,320
So you do want to do
some sort of consistency

1300
00:58:06,320 --> 00:58:08,940
with human for preference model.

1301
00:58:08,940 --> 00:58:10,132
[INAUDIBLE]

1302
00:58:10,132 --> 00:58:12,180
It's not [? quality. ?]

1303
00:58:12,180 --> 00:58:15,360
It's not scaled to
10,000 or that level.

1304
00:58:15,360 --> 00:58:17,600
You're basically
able to do based

1305
00:58:17,600 --> 00:58:20,360
on such compositional
principles.

1306
00:58:26,600 --> 00:58:30,120
So overall, in terms of results,
what this roughly means is that,

1307
00:58:30,120 --> 00:58:33,500
if you were to plot the
harmlessness Elo on y-axis

1308
00:58:33,500 --> 00:58:36,280
and the helpfulness
