are out of the box today.

1377
01:01:39,120 --> 01:01:41,160
But this is the
building block of how

1378
01:01:41,160 --> 01:01:44,960
to get the language models to
combine reasoning and acting.

1379
01:01:44,960 --> 01:01:48,680
A second aspect that we covered
today was this notion of RLEF.

1380
01:01:48,680 --> 01:01:54,480
So in coding agents, getting the
models to act in the correct way

1381
01:01:54,480 --> 01:01:56,460
requires some form of
execution feedback,

1382
01:01:56,460 --> 01:01:58,920
and you want to
iteratively incorporate

1383
01:01:58,920 --> 01:02:02,260
that feedback so that you
can generate the right code

1384
01:02:02,260 --> 01:02:03,000
solutions.

1385
01:02:03,000 --> 01:02:05,560
For code, one of the best
ways to get execution feedback

1386
01:02:05,560 --> 01:02:08,100
ends up being tests, unit tests.

1387
01:02:08,100 --> 01:02:13,060
So that's one way the models
have been used to self-improve,

1388
01:02:13,060 --> 01:02:17,960
and this also reduces the
amount of budget you need to get

1389
01:02:17,960 --> 01:02:21,240
the models to get better and
get state-of-the-art performance

1390
01:02:21,240 --> 01:02:24,980
in, say, CodeContests, and other
competitive programming tasks.

1391
01:02:24,980 --> 01:02:29,060
So that's one aspect of just
getting execution feedback

1392
01:02:29,060 --> 01:02:30,485
in the coding domain.

1393
01:02:30,485 --> 01:02:31,860
And then finally,
what we covered

1394
01:02:31,860 --> 01:02:33,360
was this notion of
constitutional AI

1395
01:02:33,360 --> 01:02:35,240
where we are getting
the model to follow

1396
01:02:35,240 --> 01:02:37,740
a set of constitutions, which
is a set of principles written

1397
01:02:37,740 --> 01:02:41,860
by humans, to generate
feedback for self-improvement.

1398
01:02:41,860 --> 01:02:44,180
In general, you can also
generalize it to anything

1399
01:02:44,180 --> 01:02:46,815
where you can get the model
to follow a set of rules.

1400
01:02:46,815 --> 01:02:49,440
And then based on whether it's
following the rules well or not,

1401
01:02:49,440 --> 01:02:51,940
you can get a
self-improvement loop going.

1402
01:02:51,940 --> 01:02:54,960
So hopefully, with
these set of papers,

1403
01:02:54,960 --> 01:02:57,740
you got a sense of how
we can build a feedback

1404
01:02:57,740 --> 01:02:59,240
loop on top of the models.

1405
01:02:59,240 --> 01:03:01,960
And when the feedback
loop has enough signal,

1406
01:03:01,960 --> 01:03:06,580
then you have a way to improve
the model beyond just what is

1407
01:03:06,580 --> 01:03:09,140
the data it was trained on.

1408
01:03:09,140 --> 01:03:11,420
And these were several
examples of where this

1409
01:03:11,420 --> 01:03:13,860
has been shown to work well.

